# Text files are stored and checked out with LF only.
#
# `core.autocrlf=input` still leaves a checkout with whatever line endings the
# file happens to have on disk, so a file edited by an editor that writes CRLF
# would come back as CRLF for everyone and show up as a whole-file diff. This
# pins the convention instead of relying on each machine's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Archives and pictures are bytes, not text: never normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.rar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
